Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• "FEATURE_NAME": Gene symbol needed for ranking differences.  
• "X_VALUE": Expression value to average.  
• "SEX": Phenotypic sex used to separate male / female cells.  
• "CELL_TYPE_COARSE": To restrict to “Epithelial” cells.  
• "CLUSTERS": To restrict to the epithelial sub‑cluster “41”.  
• "DEVELOPMENT_STAGE": Free‑text development stage; use fuzzy filter for “74‑year”.  
• "DEVELOPMENT_STAGE_ONTOLOGY_TERM_ID": Alternate coded form; inspect to see which HsapDv code maps to 74‑year‑old stage.  
• "CELL_TYPE_GENERAL", "CELL_TYPE", "CELL_TYPE_MED": Optional cross‑checks that the selection is really epithelial.  

Typical filter conditions that can be combined  
• WHERE "CELL_TYPE_COARSE" = 'Epithelial'  
•   AND "CLUSTERS" = '41'  
•   AND "DEVELOPMENT_STAGE" ILIKE '%74-year%'        -- or use matching ontology code once confirmed  
•   AND "SEX" IN ('Male','Female')  

Ten step‑wise Snowflake SQL queries (all limited to 20 rows)  
```sql
-- 1. Description: show distinct coarse cell types to verify “Epithelial” exists
SELECT DISTINCT "CELL_TYPE_COARSE"
FROM HTAN_2.HTAN.SCRNASEQ_MSK_SCLC_COMBINED_SAMPLES_CURRENT
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: list distinct cluster labels for epithelial cells
SELECT DISTINCT "CLUSTERS"
FROM HTAN_2.HTAN.SCRNASEQ_MSK_SCLC_COMBINED_SAMPLES_CURRENT
WHERE "CELL_TYPE_COARSE" = 'Epithelial'
ORDER BY "CLUSTERS"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: examine available text development stages that contain “year”
SELECT DISTINCT "DEVELOPMENT_STAGE"
FROM HTAN_2.HTAN.SCRNASEQ_MSK_SCLC_COMBINED_SAMPLES_CURRENT
WHERE "DEVELOPMENT_STAGE" ILIKE '%year%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: inspect ontology codes linked to “74‑year” (if any)
SELECT DISTINCT "DEVELOPMENT_STAGE", "DEVELOPMENT_STAGE_ONTOLOGY_TERM_ID"
FROM HTAN_2.HTAN.SCRNASEQ_MSK_SCLC_COMBINED_SAMPLES_CURRENT
WHERE "DEVELOPMENT_STAGE" ILIKE '%74-year%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: count epithelial cells in cluster 41 by sex for 74‑year‑old stage
SELECT "SEX", COUNT(*) AS "n_cells"
FROM HTAN_2.HTAN.SCRNASEQ_MSK_SCLC_COMBINED_SAMPLES_CURRENT
WHERE "CELL_TYPE_COARSE" = 'Epithelial'
  AND "CLUSTERS" = '41'
  AND "DEVELOPMENT_STAGE" ILIKE '%74-year%'
GROUP BY "SEX"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: preview expression records (gene, X_VALUE) for selected cohort
SELECT "FEATURE_NAME", "SEX", "X_VALUE"
FROM HTAN_2.HTAN.SCRNASEQ_MSK_SCLC_COMBINED_SAMPLES_CURRENT
WHERE "CELL_TYPE_COARSE" = 'Epithelial'
  AND "CLUSTERS" = '41'
  AND "DEVELOPMENT_STAGE" ILIKE '%74-year%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: compute average X_VALUE per gene & sex in cluster 41, 74‑year stage
SELECT "FEATURE_NAME",
       "SEX",
       AVG("X_VALUE") AS "avg_expr"
FROM HTAN_2.HTAN.SCRNASEQ_MSK_SCLC_COMBINED_SAMPLES_CURRENT
WHERE "CELL_TYPE_COARSE" = 'Epithelial'
  AND "CLUSTERS" = '41'
  AND "DEVELOPMENT_STAGE" ILIKE '%74-year%'
GROUP BY "FEATURE_NAME", "SEX"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: pivot the averages to put male / female on same row
SELECT "FEATURE_NAME",
       AVG(CASE WHEN "SEX" = 'Female' THEN "X_VALUE" END) AS "avg_female",
       AVG(CASE WHEN "SEX" = 'Male'   THEN "X_VALUE" END) AS "avg_male"
FROM HTAN_2.HTAN.SCRNASEQ_MSK_SCLC_COMBINED_SAMPLES_CURRENT
WHERE "CELL_TYPE_COARSE" = 'Epithelial'
  AND "CLUSTERS" = '41'
  AND "DEVELOPMENT_STAGE" ILIKE '%74-year%'
GROUP BY "FEATURE_NAME"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: calculate female–male difference and keep genes present in both sexes
WITH gene_avg AS (
  SELECT "FEATURE_NAME",
         AVG(CASE WHEN "SEX" = 'Female' THEN "X_VALUE" END) AS "avg_female",
         AVG(CASE WHEN "SEX" = 'Male'   THEN "X_VALUE" END) AS "avg_male"
  FROM HTAN_2.HTAN.SCRNASEQ_MSK_SCLC_COMBINED_SAMPLES_CURRENT
  WHERE "CELL_TYPE_COARSE" = 'Epithelial'
    AND "CLUSTERS" = '41'
    AND "DEVELOPMENT_STAGE" ILIKE '%74-year%'
  GROUP BY "FEATURE_NAME"
)
SELECT "FEATURE_NAME",
       "avg_female",
       "avg_male",
       ("avg_female" - "avg_male") AS "diff_female_minus_male"
FROM gene_avg
WHERE "avg_female" IS NOT NULL AND "avg_male" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: final query – return the top 20 genes with the greatest female‑minus‑male difference
WITH gene_avg AS (
  SELECT "FEATURE_NAME",
         AVG(CASE WHEN "SEX" = 'Female' THEN "X_VALUE" END) AS "avg_female",
         AVG(CASE WHEN "SEX" = 'Male'   THEN "X_VALUE" END) AS "avg_male"
  FROM HTAN_2.HTAN.SCRNASEQ_MSK_SCLC_COMBINED_SAMPLES_CURRENT
  WHERE "CELL_TYPE_COARSE" = 'Epithelial'
    AND "CLUSTERS" = '41'
    AND "DEVELOPMENT_STAGE" ILIKE '%74-year%'
  GROUP BY "FEATURE_NAME"
)
SELECT "FEATURE_NAME",
       "avg_female",
       "avg_male",
       ("avg_female" - "avg_male") AS "diff_female_minus_male"
FROM gene_avg
WHERE "avg_female" IS NOT NULL AND "avg_male" IS NOT NULL
ORDER BY "diff_female_minus_male" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```
